    dev_err(dev, "couldn't find required endpoints\n");
    return -ENODEV;
}
Reason:
These lines validate the presence of the expected bulk and interrupt endpoints early in the probe function, before any endpoint-dependent operations (like `kaweth_reset`). This prevents the driver from binding to devices that lack the required endpoints, thereby avoiding crashes from dereferencing missing endpoint descriptors.

